s). I retried once and the rollout completed. Post-rollback status: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and was not redeployed. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure before re-releasing."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. Before retrying, I'll check whether it was created, so I don't page on-call twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JZb9FB3QjR9mXU3SDygSvf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and is healthy again (error rate 0.18 \u2192 0.002). The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions. I retried once and it completed across us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open the incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found INC-0001 already created with the SEV2 severity and the summary of the rollback, so I did not create a duplicate. The summary notes the partial rollout failure.\n- **Not done:** I did not redeploy v2.3.1 or touch the staging v2.3.1-rc build.\n\nThe follow-up items are to investigate why v2.3.1 failed health checks and why the orchestrator halted the first rollout.", "type": "text"}]}]}